00:43:18.000 --> 00:44:06.000
There was like a blackout saying, Arbite Machtfrey works at Sufri. So she was very surprised with that slogan at the gate of the Auschwitz camp and asked me about it and I said, why don't you look it up. Hanan learned the meaning of the cynical phrase. The Jewish prisoners who entered this camp were not set free by work. They were worked to death or killed. There was this big room which had toilets and we were told that every morning more than 2,000 people gathered in front of the room and then they are given ten seconds to use it and then

72
00:44:06.000 --> 00:44:37.000
they have to leave. And so it was such a humiliation for the individual. They were things they never heard of in terms of how human beings were humiliated and broken. As they walked through the camp, Muhammad noticed that Hanan and the other students were no longer seeing the Holocaust through the lens of their own suffering. They were actually empathizing with Jews, their enemies. It was very emotional to them,

